{"title":"2013 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 5a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(faster)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (faster)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_5a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Tanner has two identical dice. Each die has six faces which are numbered 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13. When Tanner rolls the two dice, what is the probability that the sum of the numbers on the top faces is a prime number?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_5a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can list all the sums for all the possible pairs, and divide the number of sums that are prime by the total number of possible rolls. This can be done through a table or by listing everything out:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e6fe0d6361344356eb49dcd71a550c665faac2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />. This is not prime because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/27803b32e1de1532968c2bc198dd16b640f3e4b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 3 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. This is prime, so we don't skip it. This gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> combinations of rolls that give primes so far.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cda1a27fa2e448ac727bb0425727c1e5b22bb6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 5 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. This is prime, so we don't skip it. This gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more combinations of rolls that give primes, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> prime combinations of rolls that have prime sums so far.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/b/8fb6c6e68c8ae79fd2ba4062634fa95b214a8035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 7 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />. This is not prime because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/d/9fd39a072f340a5a9f39979e27bfbc3315179a6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 11 = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />. This is prime, so we don't skip it. This gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more combinations of rolls that give primes, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> prime combinations of rolls that have prime sums so far.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78730cd360425be5514b31a6256ed1794d8be551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 13 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. This is not prime because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e1a7f4874925e5df19990fe6f922b0cb3181907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 3 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. This is not prime because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/108880936ebf093c88308f58baa4abe040466366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 5 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />. This is not prime because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/4/6845da8ef8a2820b712c96fb513a53d20c9af197.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 7 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />. This is not prime because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/1/2e1c8dd27f2e3c359a1717e9241710f9ce8bf932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 11 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. This is not prime because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/0/5a06b78f5e5bce3d66ff4ccfd557470bc6be4f8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 13 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />. This is not prime because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2db1f00de266bd67fdc8a4b82718454e40a7ebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 5 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />. We have already concluded that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is composite, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/e/e8e87523e5da9ba074a78f8356e234da443043be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 7 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />. This is not prime because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/1395ff2711f131beb3c97b56e181c174fe68f800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 11 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. We have already concluded that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is composite, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/7/0672a4bb8d5c9dfe3247e284f5c1e8991e285167.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 13 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. This is not prime because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61fd6faa4e8b9ffc9a63b3737fd0fcbe4be54770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 + 7 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />. We have already concluded that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is composite, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d871163e7592bb632c108dc1d560b2cbc6fa353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 + 11 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. We have already concluded that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is composite, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/7048ec3f5ff57ef2ce8fb25cb431cb12a17ec9d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 + 13 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. This is not prime because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35ae8b987af6a7420b9fa1a0c25cb371e3bd60fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 + 11 = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />. This is not prime because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed392cebe0ac153112af9cfdd533b212c1bae0de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 + 13 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />. This is not prime because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we skip it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/c/c4c72d1a3deb98201a6a28543d6ab77ca3b60892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 + 13 = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />. This is not prime because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so we skip it.\n</p><p>We see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> combinations of rolls because each roll has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/7/3c7acc22238aff3181b71cf19ae8706f56311c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{2} = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> possible combinations of rolls. There were also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> combinations of rolls that had a prime sum.\n</p><p>Thus, the probability of getting a prime sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/5/285e16e36a065464e8d6384689095d6a06b38d18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{36} = \\boxed{\\frac16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"73\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28faster.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(faster)\">Solution 2 (faster)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_5a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (faster)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be one of the rolls because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e6fe0d6361344356eb49dcd71a550c665faac2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> is the smallest possible roll, but there are no even prime numbers greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the only even die number. If there were two odd numbers chosen, then the sum would be even.\n</p><p>Since each die has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> faces, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/242bade7eecb8dbe7d1ef62e8008cfb581dbe77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2 = 36$\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> possible combinations of rolls.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/27803b32e1de1532968c2bc198dd16b640f3e4b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 3 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cda1a27fa2e448ac727bb0425727c1e5b22bb6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 5 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/b/8fb6c6e68c8ae79fd2ba4062634fa95b214a8035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 7 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/d/9fd39a072f340a5a9f39979e27bfbc3315179a6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 11 = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78730cd360425be5514b31a6256ed1794d8be551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 13 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Of these rolls, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/2/862d4aa8a195ae71a271f6e061af41aa1d4e6e8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/2/29286174cbbd7de6698aae9f18900476d6c684f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e794a845fa296342f2054cc664b969a124f7eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> are prime. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/b/8fb6c6e68c8ae79fd2ba4062634fa95b214a8035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 7 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78730cd360425be5514b31a6256ed1794d8be551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 13 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> is divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so they are both composite. We can also switch the numbers around because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is not equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so this gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/8/e28d1e652b6dc015f8ca44794e86577f322810a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 2 = 6$\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" /> combinations of rolls where the sum would be a prime number.\n</p><p>Thus, the probability of getting a prime sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/5/285e16e36a065464e8d6384689095d6a06b38d18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{36} = \\boxed{\\frac16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"73\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232415\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 453/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17064/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.968      1 2013_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_4\n100.00%    5.968      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36043:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017232415 and revision id 279727. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}